meta {
  name: Campaign Reclassify (dry run)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/internal/campaign-reclassify
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  x-internal-secret: {{internalServiceSecret}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "meta_campaign_id": "23851234567890123",
    "campaign_type_id": "{{campaignTypeId}}",
    "dry_run": true
  }
}

docs {
  Service-to-service only -- call leads-service DIRECTLY (not through the
  gateway), authenticated by the shared internal secret.

  Returns the impact counts and writes NOTHING. This is what powers the impact
  preview in the admin's confirm dialog, and it shares its counting queries
  with the real run so the preview cannot promise something different from what
  gets confirmed.

  meta_campaign_id is a STRING: Meta campaign ids run to 17 digits, past
  Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER, so a JSON number arrives already corrupted.

  dry_run defaults to TRUE when omitted -- forgetting the flag gives a preview,
  not an unrequested fan-out across every branch.
}
